{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>Or broken.</b> Just as there, broken arm or broken leg are blemishes visible on the outside, so too here, a broken rib is excluded, for its blemish is not visible on the outside." "<b>חרוץ (split).</b> Cut, as in ״כן משפטך אתה חרצת.״" "<b>יבלת.</b> From where do we derive to apply to an animal what is stated regarding a person, and to a person what is stated regarding an animal? Scripture says ״גרב גרב״ and ״ילפת ילפת״ — for a gezeirah shavah." "<b>You shall not offer.</b> If the reason were the prohibition of בל תקדיש, it has already been stated; rather, this comes only for the prohibition of בל תשחט."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:14:23.170454316Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}